	{ 352, "34020, [cmplx], CktElement.TotalPowers, Returns a pointer to an array of complex with the the total powers (complex) at ALL terminals of the active circuit element. Each element is a complex structure including real and imaginary parts (double, 16 Bytes per element)." },
	{ 353, "34021, [int], CktElement.Open, This parameter opens the specified terminal and phase of the active circuit element. The caller must provide the Pointer argument as a byte array containing two 32-bit integers: the first representing the terminal and the second indicating the phase. Returns a pointer to an array of integer. The first element of the array would be 1 if the opening was unsuccessful, 0 otherwise." },
	{ 354, "34022, [int], CktElement.Close, This parameter closes the specified terminal and phase of the active circuit element. The caller must provide the Pointer argument as a byte array containing two 32-bit integers: the first representing the terminal and the second indicating the phase. Returns a pointer to an array of integer. The first element of the array would be 0 if the closing was unsuccessful, 1 otherwise." },
	{ 355, "34023, [int], CktElement.IsOpen, This parameter queries whether a specific terminal and phase of the active circuit element is open. If the phase value is zero, the function checks whether any phase at the terminal is open. The caller must provide a Pointer argument, which references a byte array containing two 32-bit integers: the first representing the terminal and the second indicating the phase. Returns a pointer to an array of integer. The result is stored in the first element of the array, with false represented as 0." },
	{ 356, "34024, [cmplx], CktElement.AllLosses - read, Returns a pointer to an array of complex with all power losses in the active circuit element in the following order: Total losses, load losses and no-load losses. Each element is a complex structure including real and imaginary parts (double, 16 Bytes per element)." },
