	{ 983, "116040, int, Solution.TotalIterations, This parameter returns the total iterations including control iterations for most recent solution." },
	{ 984, "116041, int, Solution.MostIterationsDone, This parameter returns the max number of iterations required to converge at any control iteration of the most recent solution." },
	{ 985, "116042, int, Solution.ControlActionsDone - read, This parameter indicates that the control actions are done: {1 done, 0 not done}." },
	{ 986, "116043, int, Solution.ControlActionsDone - write, This parameter modifies the flag to indicate that the control actions are done: {1 done, 0 not done}." },
	{ 987, "116044, int, Solution.FinishTimeStep, This parameter calls cleanup, sample monitors, and increment time at end of time step." },
	{ 988, "116045, int, Solution.Cleanup, This parameter update storage, invcontrol, etc., at end of time step." },
	{ 989, "116046, int, Solution.SolveAll, This parameter starts the solution process for all the actors created in memory. Please be sure that the circuits of each actor have been compiled and ready to be solved before using this command." },
	{ 990, "116047, int, Solution.CalcIncMatrix, This parameter starts the calculation of the incidence matrix for the active actor. Please be sure that the circuits of each actor have been compiled and ready to be solved before using this command." },
	{ 991, "116048, int, Solution.CalcIncMatrix_O, This parameter starts the calculation of the Branch to Node incidence matrix for the active actor. Please be sure that the circuits of each actor have been compiled and ready to be solved before using this command. The difference between this command and the CalcIncMatrix is that the calculated matrix will be ordered hierarchically from the substation to the feeder end, which can be helpful for many operations. Additionally, the Bus Levels vector is calculated and the rows (PDElements) and columns (Buses) are permuted so it is easy to identify their position in the circuit." },
	{ 992, "116049, int, Solution.SolveSnap, This method executes the snapshot power flow routine in the DSS that solves the present state with control actions." },
	{ 993, "116050, int, Solution.MinIterations - read, This property Gets the minimum number of iterations required for a solution. Default is 2." },
	{ 994, "116051, int, Solution.MinIterations - write, This property Sets the minimum number of iterations required for a solution. Default is 2." },
